## Primary Goal
I want to create a German-language online search application for social work. It should list local social services and support offers for clients.

The interface should be simple and accessible, with large, easy-to-read text and color-blind-friendly design. The app should have two areas: a public search function and a password-protected admin area. In the admin area, the password can be changed and the database edited. The database is an Excel spreadsheet provided during development. The initial password is “katze”.

Users should enter their postal code and desired search radius in kilometers.

The admin area should include a ChatGPT integration that searches the web for relevant Google entries and saves results into an Excel table based on a predefined schema. The schema should be requested beforehand, with categories used as column names. It must be clearly shown that AI-generated results require verification. New results should automatically replace the previous dataset.

